            <div xml:id="d727-a3">

                <pb facs="0867" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg765"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister O’Brien to the Chairman of the Revolutionary
                        Committee.</hi></head>
                <p>The American minister, dean of the diplomatic corps, in his own name and in the
                    name of his colleagues, salutes Senor don Adolfo Riquélme, and has the honor to
                    communicate to him that the representatives of nations friendly to Paraguay have
                    resolved that under the supposition of the possible triumph of those who have
                    risen against the Government, they will, for the honor of this nation, place
                    under their protection the persons of the head of the State, his ministers, and
                    other high functionaries.</p>
                <p>Feeling certain that it is the intention of the revolutionary committee of which
                    he is the head to act in the same spirit of humanity, he begs to suggest both
                    privately and officially that all efforts may be made to bring about such a
                    desideratum for the welfare and dignity of the country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Hotel Hispano Americano,
                            <placeName>Asuncion</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-07-03">July 3, 1908</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward C. O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
